# Cloud Agent prompts (promt.md)

When authoring **`promt.md`** (or any paste-ready Cloud Agent task), **always** include a **Git / AutoReview workflow** block. Cloud agents tend to push many small commits; Cursor AutoReview often runs **once per push** and may lag or miss rapid-fire commits.

## Commit strategy (pick one — state it explicitly in the prompt)

### A) Single commit at the end (recommended)

1. Do all work locally — **no push** until functionally done.
2. Run checks (`npm run check`, `check:rust`, lint, smoke) locally.
3. **One** commit (or squash locally) → **one push** → open/update PR.
4. **Wait for AutoReview** (see below) before declaring “ready to merge”.

### B) Multiple commits allowed

After **each push**:

1. Wait **≥ 10 minutes** for AutoReview on the **latest** commit SHA.
2. Poll PR reviews / comments for `CURSOR_AUTOMATION_ID` / “Sent by Cursor Automation: AutoReview”.
3. If AutoReview comments on an **older** SHA — either wait for a re-run on HEAD or push an empty/amend **only if** fixes are needed.
4. If **no** AutoReview after 10 min — note in PR comment; owner may trigger **TEST** manually in Cursor Automations.
5. **Do not** push again while AutoReview on HEAD is still pending unless fixing a blocker it reported.

## AutoReview block (copy into every promt.md)

```markdown
## Git & AutoReview (mandatory)

- One PR; **do not merge yourself**.
- Prefer **one final commit + one push** when work is complete.
- After the final push: wait up to **10 minutes** for AutoReview on **HEAD**.
- Final PR comment must cite: last commit SHA, AutoReview status (green / manual TEST / pending), CI status.
- If AutoReview is red — fix and push once; wait again.
- Do not stack 3+ commits in 30 seconds — AutoReview may only review the last push or skip triggers.
```

## AutoReview not firing automatically

If automation is enabled but only **TEST + PR URL** works:

- Re-check Cursor Automation trigger: **PR synchronize / push to PR branch**, not “PR opened” only.
- Re-authorize **Cursor GitHub App** on `ebluffy/Owyx` (repo rename breaks webhooks).
- Ensure PR is from a branch in the same repo (not fork without app access).

Document findings in PR comment; do not block on automation if CI + self-review are green and owner ran manual TEST.
